{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics","id":1467466,"title":"Alternative Hermetics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-11T13:04:19-08:00","id":1467466,"title":"Alternative Hermetics?","content":"What do you think the Hermetic Tradition would look like, had there not been an <i>Ars Magica</i>? Would there even be one?<br /> <br /> To expand a little, something always bothered me about the Hermetics. Their paradigm discussion always seemed a little thin; like they're the Western esoteric tradition... except there's not a great deal of discussion of it. They have this house structure which whilst cool feels more like Harry Potter than the Golden Dawn.<br /> <br /> Then, I actually read <i>Ars Magica</i> and it kinda made sense. Like, the Order was written with this really quasi-fantasy setting in mind; where the different houses are really more like separate traditions of magic than a unified group. Like, they have a 'hermetic theory' that they more or less agree on, but it's not really expanded on much.<br /> <br /> Basically, it now feels like the original creators just lifted the Order from <i>Ars</i> and placed it down in Ascension and called it a day... Which, I get. It makes perfect to carry it over. However, I can't get rid of the feeling that it's really constrained the Tradition since then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:20:59-08:00","id":1467470,"title":"","content":"They did. And there was an edition of Ars Magica that tweet setting ever so slightly to bring it more in line with the world of darkness. <br /> <br /> The thing is, the original Traditions we're mostly built around archetypes. You had your Martial artist, your priest, your ecstatic, your shaman, your necromancer, your wizard, your mad scientist, your witch, and your hacker. Since then, all of them have been given additional depth. Including, yes, the Order of Hermes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:45:55-08:00","id":1467474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467470#post1467470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did. And there was an edition of Ars Magica that tweet setting ever so slightly to bring it more in line with the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that was after they'd already created Ascension, and didn't really deal with the Order being... well, not really very 'hermetic' or 'western esoteric'. Like Ars is basically a historical setting with fantasy wizards in it. I'm not saying that it's bad, just not what Ascension really seems to be going for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, the original Traditions we're mostly built around archetypes. You had your Martial artist, your priest, your ecstatic, your shaman, your necromancer, your wizard, your mad scientist, your witch, and your hacker. Since then, all of them have been given additional depth. Including, yes, the Order of Hermes. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but my point is that the Order aren't really an archetype. They're an organisation from a different game that were incorporated into Ascension as if they were an archetype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:09:25-08:00","id":1467475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467474#post1467474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but my point is that the Order aren't really an archetype. They're an organisation from a different game that were incorporated into Ascension as if they were an archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's both. If I'm not mistaken, Ars Magica was stated to be (among other things) an attempt to make wizards w/o the &quot;artificial&quot; old DnD limitations to balance them (inhability to use certain weapons and armor, less hp than other humans, etc...)<br /> <br /> It really is an archetype, and always was: &quot;You're a Wizard, Harry&quot;<br /> <br /> Now. How would the &quot;Disney Merlin&quot; Tradition have looked w/o <i>Ars</i>?. Well, I don't know. Perhaps they would seem like a softer and more multicultural version of the Taftani: Wizened magicians that control fire, ride magic carpets, have magick jewlery, create golems, etc? There are many ways to spin that archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-11-2021, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:16:04-08:00","id":1467477,"title":"","content":"I'm not disagreeing; that's exactly how they started out. It doesn't mean that it was a bad move, or that they need to be scrapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:25:51-08:00","id":1467478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It really is an archetype, and always was: &quot;You're a Wizard, Harry&quot; </div> </div> </div>Sure, but it's never really connected to something real in the same way the other Traditions do. I dunno, they seem different in some way. Like, the other Traditions feel like they wanted an archetype and they actually built up a structure from that, whilst the Order were just transplanted over. There's some handwaving towards Enochian and kabbalah but that's kinda it.<br /> <br /> Actually, come to think of it, the Dreamspeakers have a similar issue with carrying over Apocalypse stuff, though for whatever reason, they were more malleable than the Order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467475#post1467475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the &quot;Disney Merlin&quot; Tradition have looked w/o <i>Ars</i>?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the opposite. What would a tradition that was based on the western esoteric tradition look like?<br /> <br /> I guess maybe the Solifcati or maybe the Cosians?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:48:26-08:00","id":1467480,"title":"","content":"Very few of the Traditions started out connected to something \u201creal\u201d; nearly all of them had their ties to real world magical beliefs grafted on after the fact. As is, a lot of people have complaints about dream speakers and verbena representing the Witch and shaman archetypes far more than they do any real world beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:54:39-08:00","id":1467481,"title":"","content":"As for what they would look like without their Ars Magica origin, consider Mage: the Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-11-2021, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:55:22-08:00","id":1467482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467478#post1467478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but it's never really connected to something real in the same way the other Traditions do. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know, I have similar issues with the Chorus and Verbena. It would be interesting to take all three of them and build them up from first principles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:02:41-08:00","id":1467483,"title":"","content":"And the akashic brotherhood could use some work on being something more than just \u201cthe Monks\u201d. I have already mentioned the Dreamspeakers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:03:41-08:00","id":1467484,"title":"","content":"There were Hermetic Magi. John Dee was a fine example. Among other things he introduced the division \u2797 symbol and the equals = sign to the English speaking world. Dee was also the first person to propose teaching ship's navigators math. <br /> <br /> Science, or as they called it natural philosophy, didn't fully exclude magic until the late 17th century. Issac Newton was far more a Magus than a scientist. French scientific journals excepted articles on Alchemy until almost the 1750s.<br /> <br /> Hermeticism seems to start in the decades after the death of Alexander the Great. The idea was that all humans have a spark of Divinity (in game the Avatar). By developing your inner spark of Divinity you could become godlike or even a god. Apollonisus of Tyana was a real Hermetic Magus who was worshipped as a god. <br /> <br /> Hermeticism was real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:19:58-08:00","id":1467488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467478#post1467478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the opposite. What would a tradition that was based on the western esoteric tradition look like?<br /> <br /> I guess maybe the Solifcati or maybe the Cosians?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order of Reason it's not a bad place to start such speculation, but you would need more than those two. The Solificati are just alchemy and the Cosians are hyper-focused on the body. You would need to include things like sacred geometry, angelic/demonic summonings, astrology, etc. At the end I think you would find the result looks a lot like the OoH, perhaps with less pointy hats (that were a wrong stereotype IOC anyway)<br /> <br /> On a more general note: I think you're mistaken in thinking &quot;wizards&quot; are less *based* than the &quot;mystical orient&quot; or &quot;shamans&quot;. I think that depends on how one goes about it.<br /> <br /> For instance: I would argue that Akashicks are to Buddhists and Taoists what the Order of Hermes it's to the Golden Down: The first it's &quot;magick kung fu&quot;, the latter it's using words of power to summon thunder - in both cases it's taking ideas that do come from real life, but that are considered fantastical. The very name of the Akashicks comes from the Akashic Record, wich it's an invention of &quot;orientalism&quot;. Taking all of that in consideration I thin Hermetics can be forgiven for being more fantastical than the real Golden Down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:38:46-08:00","id":1467489,"title":"","content":"Their emphasis on the power of spoken words lines up well with Forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T17:14:42-08:00","id":1467501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467482#post1467482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t know, I have similar issues with the Chorus</div> </div> </div> </div>My first impression of an idea that the Celestial Chorus don't seem connected to something real is that it would be a testament to how effectively Roman Catholicism wiped out Christian denominations with a more mystical bent, or otherwise significantly divergent views about the nature of Jesus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T17:44:41-08:00","id":1467503,"title":"","content":"I have to mention the introduction of Eliphas Levi's book of &quot;dogma and rituals of high magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> In concrete, the pages 10-11. It has a list of the powers and privileges of the &quot;wise man&quot; that holds the Clavicles of Solomon in his right hand. You know, it's small realistic stuff like: &quot;Behold God face to face w/o dying and converse with the genii who command the entire celestial army&quot;, &quot;rules the elements, stills tempests, cures diseased by the touch and raises the dead&quot;, &quot;pronounce those words that paralize and charm serpents&quot;. &quot;knows the key of inmortality&quot;, &quot;He reigns with all heaven and is served by all hell&quot;...<br /> <br /> From a purely aesthetical perspective: <i>very </i>OoH , isn't it? (well, they wish :P ). It does inspire in me the idea of the &quot;Wizard Archetype&quot; seeking absolute power trough research of forbidden knowledge, that's also the archetype of DnD and other fantasy stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-11-2021, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T18:38:32-08:00","id":1467506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467501#post1467501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first impression of an idea that the Celestial Chorus don't seem connected to something real is that it would be a testament to how effectively Roman Catholicism wiped out Christian denominations with a more mystical bent, or otherwise significantly divergent views about the nature of Jesus.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they were a collection of Christian denominations with a mystical bent, I would agree, but they are more a proto-theosophic secret society that hides within the major monotheistic religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T04:53:21-08:00","id":1467536,"title":"","content":"One thing that might be helpful. The image of the &quot;wise old man who pulled secret and powerful information out of dusty tomes that lesser men could not understand&quot; is not the product of a secret order but a mainstream and relatively accurate description of the state of Western Europe in the 900 year period between the fall of the Roman Empire and the Renaissance. During that time, advanced knowledge came from writings of the past and was often hidden in surviving texts in languages that most people couldn't speak or read. <br /> <br /> Amusingly, some of this inaccessible knowledge included old Roman law, which turned out to be very powerful and useful despite no longer being in effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T06:49:59-08:00","id":1467555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467478#post1467478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but it's never really connected to something real in the same way the other Traditions do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think it is more connected to something real and specific than any other Tradition,<br /> <br /> The OoH isn't so much Golden Down, but mainly Thelema. Actually it is a lot of Thelema. It is a loose reference to the history of Hermeticism in Europe, but tweaked to be viewed exclusively through the lens of Thelema.<br /> <br /> Some of their distinction is also lost in the way they achieved to make the entire Council of Nine Traditions follow their teachings, so part of what does make the Hermetics Hermetics became mandatory teaching in the entire organization.<br /> <br /> Which is a Watsonian result from the Doylist decision of using Thelema-like philosophy as the basis for the entire game line, so the Order of Hermes is, for all purposes and intents, especially in 1st edition, <b>objectively right</b>.<br /> <br /> If you assume that most of the objective truths of the setting aren't actually objective truths, but Hermetic theory, then their particularities become more apparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T12:00:27-08:00","id":1467585,"title":"","content":"<br /> Most of the Traditions do make more sense within the philosophies of the 20th century than the philosophies of the 15th. Unsurprising since they were imagined in light of the former and then backdated. <br /> <br /> I suppose if I were going to rethink the OoH, I'd focus on hermeticism and the search for ancient knowledge and drop the early formation of 'houses' and such. The Tradition would likely grow out of the informal correspondences of scribes and researchers that also gave rise to modern science. The houses would form significantly later, likely between the 13th and 17th centuries, around the time that the bounds of human knowledge started getting pushed forward again (in Europe) in our world. When the houses did arise they would probably be called schools or societies, since that's what they'd be: associations of scholars into competing and cooperating schools of thought. <br /> <br /> Despite matching much of the history of the development of science and philosophy these schools would have very similar character to what we think of in the OoH. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> pointed out, Newton and his contemporaries were much more magically inclined than we think of. My go-to example is that Rene Descartes believed that a drum made from lambskin would not make a sound in the presence of a drum made of wolf skin. This being Mage we can also presume that there was both more mystical knowledge to be preserved and more effort to preserve it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T13:12:52-08:00","id":1467596,"title":"","content":"I actually realised, I already kinda have an answer to my question. From way back in 1992 or so on Usenet, presumably before the original OoH book, the Ander's Mage Page website has/had a bunch of sub-traditions for the Order that were based on different aspects of the Western esoteric tradition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467483#post1467483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the akashic brotherhood could use some work on being something more than just \u201cthe Monks\u201d. I have already mentioned the Dreamspeakers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely could. However, I'd say Revised does a lot within the restrictions it's given. I think the issue is kinda that the game has been very reluctant to actually retcon stuff. Like, the Shi-Ren are miles away from the warrior-monk origin point... but they still have to practice do.<br /> <br /> I think my major issue with the Order is that the house structure is so important to the Order that it seems to seriously limit the ability to differentiate different Hermetic sub-factions. However, yeah, I think it's an issue for basically all of the groups in Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T15:55:10-08:00","id":1467607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467596#post1467596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually realised, I already kinda have an answer to my question. From way back in 1992 or so on Usenet, presumably before the original OoH book, the Ander's Mage Page website has/had a bunch of sub-traditions for the Order that were based on different aspects of the Western esoteric tradition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They absolutely could. However, I'd say Revised does a lot within the restrictions it's given. I think the issue is kinda that the game has been very reluctant to actually retcon stuff. Like, the Shi-Ren are miles away from the warrior-monk origin point... but they still have to practice do.<br /> <br /> I think my major issue with the Order is that the house structure is so important to the Order that it seems to seriously limit the ability to differentiate different Hermetic sub-factions. However, yeah, I think it's an issue for basically all of the groups in Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! I think I see what you're complaint is now. It's not that the order of Hermes isn't rooted in Western esoterica; it's that it's various factions don't serve as a breakdown of what those Western esoterica are. They're more political than anything else.<br /> <br /> And that's not a bad thing anymore, IMHO. Not with the Traditions having been \u201cdemoted\u201d in M20 from being the \u201ckeepers of Paradigm\u201d to \u201cmerely\u201d political factions: it's no longer the default assumption that if you're a purveyor of Western esoterica, them you're in the Order of Hermes. So I'm not terribly inclined to rework the Houses anymore. <br /> <br /> But I'm okay in principle with doing so as a thought experiment. For instance, how about a seven-faction breakdown conforming to the classical planets, or a four-faction arrangement corresponding to the Elements?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T20:19:07-08:00","id":1467633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1467506#post1467506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they were a collection of Christian denominations with a mystical bent, I would agree, but they are more a proto-theosophic secret society that hides within the major monotheistic religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that I think the Celestial Chorus as I understand them resonates with some of the more out there religious beliefs that cropped up in the early eras of Christianity. <br /> <br /> In the context of Mage: the Ascension, I would think it would make sense that people who Awaken with a cultural reference point to Christianity or similar religions would be drawn to those heterodoxies over alternative mystical systems, and then it would make sense that they'd go underground in the face of things like historical persecutions enacted by Christians.<br /> <br /> It's like being reminiscent of Catharism (but going to some different places owing to being in possession of real tangible power), and keeping quiet out of consideration for what happened to the Cathars.<br /> <br /> I think that should be enough to <u>connect</u> to something that was real. I think there's a point at which wanting it to be more strongly informed by reality is departing a bit from the work of fiction.<br /> <br /> (Suddenly I'm recalling an instance in which somebody whom I believe was a writer on Mage: the Ascension said something to the effect of &quot;we wanted to write in reference to real life belief systems, but thought reproducing them wholesale would be disrespectful&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T21:47:50-08:00","id":1467639,"title":"","content":"I think it is more like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said. There's a sense of referencing but not reproducing belief systems, but mainly the &quot;problem&quot; as we may define it is that the basis for all Traditions isn't the true history of occultism, but just the occult philosophies of the 20th century.<br /> <br /> So when you go backwards in time it gets weird, as those philosophies have far less actual tradition than they purport to, or far less kinship, and so on. Like how the Dreamspeakers work under a unified theory about shamanism, but this theory is actually a modern Anthropological thesis. Some animistic groups do accept it now, but back then it doesn't really make any sense for the unified Tradition to form.<br /> <br /> To make them anew in a more sensible way we would have to start from the past and bring them, instead of the opposite direction, but that would also be a very different game in the end, as those modern philosophies did shaped a lot of what Mage became.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T07:57:49-08:00","id":1468004,"title":"","content":"Exactly. If we were to build the Chorus based on earlier philosophies they would probably be a mash up of monotheistic mage groups that banded together against a common enemy. This would likely form in earnest because of persecution from the Order of Reason, but there might be informal groundwork for this alliance back to the 4th century AD* with heretical and/or politically isolated Christian mage groups sheltering each other against persecution.<br /> <br /> *It could go back as far as the Roman mystery cults if we presume a greater degree of Roman persecutions of those entities that is historically seen.<br /> <br /> Instead they are a hypothetical ancient Egyptian monotheistic group whose core beliefs have only a vague similarity to Christianity, Islam, and other monotheistic religions, and are wildly incompatible when you dig beneath the surface. In many ways the Chorus has more in common with Baha'i or the Theosophical Society than it does with Christianity. It's a 20th Century AD organization that for some reason started in the 20th Century BC.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T08:40:35-08:00","id":1468008,"title":"","content":"But, how can they be wildly inconsistent with Christianity when they accept all monotheistic beliefs? :deadpan:<br /> <br /> But seriously, This. The Celestial Chorus could, no doubt, be reimagined in a way that's more consistent with its mostly Abrahamic trappings; but the result wouldn't be nearly as diverse as the current version. After <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> mentioned Theosophy in disguise, I decided to look into Theosophy. And you know what? He's right: change some of the details (such as having the Masters originating in the Middle East instead of Tibet, and scraping away some of the more racist elements), and it's a near-perfect match for the Celestial Chorus as written. The Celestial Chorus is every bit as much in \u201cneed\u201d of an overhaul to bring it more in line with its real-world \u201croots\u201d as the Order of Hermes is. <br /> <br /> And you can play that game with (nearly?) every Tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T09:49:59-08:00","id":1468016,"title":"","content":"Yeah I would say basically every tradition with the possible exclusion of the Society of Ether and Virtual Adepts who have been representatives of a philosophy and it\u2019s potential Awakened manifestations since word go. Not that we couldn\u2019t do a better job of depicting that, but it is an advantage they have over other traditions.<br /> <br /> The games do of course offer a retroactive explanation that at least justifies why things are so weird and jumbled but it\u2019s also something that I do think good work can be done in the revision of.<br /> <br /> (Also this is my own personal bugbear but I\u2019ve thought for a while now that if you\u2019re gonna have a monotheistic tradition then Islam would form a much better foundation culture for it then Catholic Christianity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T11:03:10-08:00","id":1468024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1468016#post1468016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also this is my own personal bugbear but I\u2019ve thought for a while now that if you\u2019re gonna have a monotheistic tradition then Islam would form a much better foundation culture for it then Catholic Christianity)</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on when they start and why. Setting aside non-Abrahamic monotheism (that is actually older, but also different).<br /> <br /> We could put the Chorus beginning with the First Council of Nicaea, as an answer against the decisions that relegated many early Christian communities and philosophers as heretics.<br /> <br /> Such version of the Chorus could be based on free acceptance and discussion of different interpretations of the faith and gather others with time. And they're possibly involved in the protection of persecuted heresies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T11:24:58-08:00","id":1468025,"title":"","content":"My own view is that if you're interested in factions that stay true to real world beliefs, you should be looking at the Disparates, not the Traditions. With a handful of exceptions, that's what the Disparates are for: fidelity to and preservation of belief systems. By contrast, up until M20, the Traditions were always portrayed as viewing there paradigms as something to be transcended. Their overall shared view was that all of them were essentially doing the same thing, differing only in terms of how they went about it. Arguably, that even applies in M20 to an extent; and in my games, I make that what defines the Traditions and sets them apart from everyone else. With that view of things, it makes sense that each tradition has deliberately cultivated as broad a base as possible. So the Celestial Chorus emphasizing inclusivity above all else, and featuring imams, rabbis, pastors, nuns, and others, up to and including the occasional white witch, strikes me as perfectly appropriate for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T12:56:32-08:00","id":1468295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467466-alternative-hermetics?p=1468024#post1468024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on when they start and why. Setting aside non-Abrahamic monotheism (that is actually older, but also different).<br /> <br /> We could put the Chorus beginning with the First Council of Nicaea, as an answer against the decisions that relegated many early Christian communities and philosophers as heretics.<br /> <br /> Such version of the Chorus could be based on free acceptance and discussion of different interpretations of the faith and gather others with time. And they're possibly involved in the protection of persecuted heresies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of historical note, that's also the Council where Santa Claus decked a heretic. By that I mean Nicholas, the Bishop of Myra and future saint, got up and slugged Arias, future heretic. I say future heretic because at the time the council hadn't declared his theology heretical and heresy isn't usually backdated. Indeed, for that reason the Council never declared Arias or his followers heretics, because what they taught wasn't, until the end of the council, a heresy. Indeed, St Nick was thrown in prison for his violence, though he was apparently freed by a Marian apparition.<br /> <br /> Bishop Nicholas went on to be canonized a saint. Arias went on to die of explosive flatulence. History is amazing sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}